From: Thingino VDB2 mechanical-chime investigation
Subject: [DIAGNOSTIC ONLY] MIPS: T31 Swan: restore PB27 boot pull-up

The recovered Wyze VDB2 stock kernel's gpio_pull_init() calls
jz_gpio_set_func(59, GPIO_PULL_UP). The corresponding generic Swan source
entry is commented in Thingino. Restore it for a controlled stock-waveform
comparison.

This patch is intentionally not selected by the VDB2 defconfig. GPIO59 is
connected to the doorbell power/chime control circuit, so the weak-high boot
interval must be electrically validated before becoming a profile default.

--- a/arch/mips/xburst/soc-t31/chip-t31/isvp/Swan/gpio_customized.c
+++ b/arch/mips/xburst/soc-t31/chip-t31/isvp/Swan/gpio_customized.c
@@ -14,8 +14,7 @@ typedef struct gpio_drive_strength_table {
 } gpio_drive_strength_table_t;

 static gpio_pull_table_t soc_gpio_pull_table[] = {
-// Don't force the pull state of the GPIO since we may not be using it for the TF cd pin
-//	{ GPIO_PB(27), GPIO_PULL_UP }, //TF cd
+	{ GPIO_PB(27), GPIO_PULL_UP }, // VDB2 stock kernel boot waveform
 };

 static gpio_drive_strength_table_t soc_gpio_drive_strength_table[] = {
